            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PatCM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The cook where I worked at my first job in 1964 used to make a big pan of Apple Pan Dowdy every day and it was a big seller. I had to try this recipe and I loved it. It's so much easier than making apple pie and tastes almost the same. The topping is poured over the apples and bakes up very much like a pie crust, but there was not enough to cover the apples in this recipe. But it tasted really good and brought back good memories. The only substitution I made was butter in the topping instead of shortening. I haven't cooked with shortening for many years. I'll be making this again."
          },
